WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.004
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Sensory Overload Reset.

00:00:14.004 --> 00:00:20.008
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:20.008 --> 00:00:23.611
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:23.611 --> 00:00:27.213
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:27.213 --> 00:00:35.619
Sometimes the world gets big. Sounds stack up. Lights feel bright. The room feels full and close.

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:45.226
When that happens, your body notices first. Ears feel full. Shoulders climb up. Everything feels like too much at once.

00:00:45.226 --> 00:00:56.034
That feeling is information, not misbehavior. Your body is saying: this is more than I can hold right now.

00:00:56.034 --> 00:01:00.837
And there is a reset for it. It has four moves. Let me show you.

00:01:00.837 --> 00:01:11.645
Move one: notice. Just name it inside: "This is too much right now." Naming it is the start.

00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:22.452
Move two: tell a grown-up. A word, a look, a raised hand — your teacher needs to know before you move. Safety first, always.

00:01:22.452 --> 00:01:33.260
Move three: shrink the input. Hands over ears is allowed. Eyes down is allowed. A quieter spot your teacher shows you is allowed.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:42.866
Move four: breathe slowly, and let the quiet do its work. There is no hurry. Quiet is not a race.

00:01:42.866 --> 00:01:44.067
When your body feels like itself again — shoulders down, ears calm — you come back. Coming back is part of the reset too.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:54.875
Stepping away to reset is a strategy. It is never a punishment, and it is never being sent away from the group.

00:01:54.875 --> 00:02:05.682
Needing quiet does not make anyone weak, or dramatic, or different in a bad way. Bodies are different. That is all.

00:02:05.682 --> 00:02:14.088
Some days the reset takes a minute. Some days it takes longer. Both are fine. Your body sets the time, nobody else.

00:02:14.088 --> 00:02:15.289
And when you come back, the room will still be here — and so will your place in it.

00:02:15.289 --> 00:02:23.695
Notice. Tell a grown-up. Shrink the input. Breathe.

00:02:23.695 --> 00:02:29.699
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:29.699 --> 00:02:34.503
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:34.503 --> 00:02:40.507
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:40.507 --> 00:02:46.511
You're ready for what's next.
